  "description": "Aliler Castle is the modern Turkish name of an Urartian fortress situated near the village of Karaa\u011fa\u00e7, approx. 11 km southeast of Lake Van. Here, the remains of a column base with a fragmentary preserved Urartian inscription of the Urartian king Minua (9th / 8th century BCE) have been found.",
